course: dictionary
lesson: 15704
title: Topaz: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around them. Topaz can mean a hard stone, one jewel made from that stone, or a golden-yellow colour. «She wore a topaz ring to the party.» You can wear a ring, so topaz is a jewel here.
explain: «Her dress was a soft topaz colour.» A dress has a colour, not a stone, so topaz means the golden-yellow colour. Always ask: which meaning fits the sentence? Then try it in place of the word and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Clues can also come from the rest of the text. If you read about a hard, shiny stone in a jewellery shop, topaz is the stone. If you read about a colour in a sunset, topaz is the colour. The context tells you which meaning to use.
fact: Topaz is a hard, clear gemstone used in jewellery.
fact: Topaz can be golden-yellow, brown, blue or pink.
fact: «A topaz» means one jewel made of this stone.
fact: On the Mohs scale of hardness, topaz is number 8, and diamond is number 10.
fact: November's birthstone is topaz, so it is linked to that month of the year.
exercise: «The jeweller polished the topaz until it sparkled.» What is a topaz in this sentence? | A kind of water | A golden-yellow colour | A type of rock dust | *One jewel made of the stone
exercise: «Her scarf was the same golden-yellow as topaz.» What does topaz mean here? | A metal | A birthday party | *A golden-yellow colour | A hard stone
exercise: Diamond is number 10 on the Mohs scale. What number is topaz? | *8 | 10 | 5 | 1
test: «The shop sold a pink topaz necklace.» Which colours can topaz stones be? | Black and grey | *Golden-yellow, brown, blue or pink | Only green | Red and white
test: Topaz is 8 on the Mohs scale and diamond is 10. Is topaz harder or softer than diamond? | Not on the scale at all | Harder | *Softer | The same
exam: «Ava's ring had a blue topaz set in silver.» What does topaz mean in this sentence? | A colour of the sky | A month of the year | *A jewel made of the stone | A type of silver
